:''Not to be confused with [[Cat Princess (Special Cat)|Cat Princess]] or [[Possessed Empress]].''
'''Princess Cat''' is an [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare Cat]] that can be unlocked by playing the [[Cat Capsule#Rare Capsule|Rare Capsule]] during the [[RoyalFest (Gacha Event)|RoyalFest]] event. She is conducting [[Empress' Research|research]] on the [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] and opened the gates to [[The Aku Realms]], eventually leading her to become [[Possessed Empress]]. She was added in [[Version 10.6 Update|Version 10.6]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 612
|rarity = UR
|name1 = Princess Cat
|name2 = Empress Cat
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Empress Cat''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Princess Cat is similar to [[Emperor Cat (Legend Rare Cat)|Emperor Cat]] for the most part. She specializes in delivering good damage from good distance, with added [[Mini-Wave]]s to further extend her reach.

Her weaken ability makes her very powerful against the traits she targets. If kept in the back and well defended, she will help protect the army and do so quite effectively, while also delivering good damage. What sets her apart from most alternatives is that the weaken can be applied to more than just the enemy frontline, leading enemy midrangers who usually avoid this effect to take it regardless.

Against Zombies, although weaken is a powerful ability to apply on an enemy who pops up in the middle of the cat army, she tends to struggle more due to her fragility and long attack rate and windup, which prevent her from shaking off threats in time.

[[Immune to Curse|Curse Immunity]] has little purpose for a backliner, but it allows her to be a decent counter against [[Loris]] in stages where he supports enemies that Princess Cat can weaken, such as [[Miracle Iris (Deadly)]].

{{Job|Classification = Super-Backliner & Crowd-Controller}}

